    <section class="bg-cream product-faq">
    <div class="container content">
      <h2>200 Ton Wash Plant — Common Questions</h2>
      <h3>How much does a 200 ton gold wash plant cost?</h3>
      <p>Every 200 Ton plant is custom-built to the ground it will run on, so we quote each one rather than publish a single list price. Build time is one to three weeks. What moves the number most is the power package, the feed setup and where it ships to. Our <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-cost-guide/">gold wash plant cost guide</a> walks through each of those, and a quote request comes back with a firm figure.</p>
      <h3>How much water does the 200 Ton need?</h3>
      <p>The 200 Ton runs at 2,200 GPM. That is the flow through the plant, not the volume you have to haul — most operations <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-water-requirements/">recirculate</a> off a settling pond, so a single water source keeps the plant producing for days. Sizing the pond and pump to your ground is part of the quote.</p>
      <h3>What powers a 200 ton wash plant?</h3>
      <p><a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-power-requirements/">Diesel or electric</a>, configured with the plant. Diesel is the usual choice on remote claims with no line power. Electric makes sense where you already have a generator set or grid supply on site.</p>
      <h3>What size rock can the 200 Ton take?</h3>
      <p>The 200 Ton handles feed up to 24 inches. Oversize is screened and rejected rather than jamming the plant, which is what keeps a plant running a full shift instead of stopping to clear a blockage. <a href="/blog/feeding-gold-wash-plant-excavator-vs-dump-truck/">How you feed it</a> matters here too.</p>
      <h3>How fine a gold will the 200 Ton hold?</h3>
      <p>The ~45 feet sluice recovers 95-98% down to 200 mesh. Recovery of very fine and <a href="/blog/fine-gold-recovery/">flour gold</a> depends as much on how the material is fed and how the sluice is run as it does on the plant itself.</p>
      <h3>Can the 200 Ton ship outside the United States?</h3>
      <p>Yes. We build in the USA and ship worldwide, and more than half of our enquiries come from outside the country. Containerisation, documentation and <a href="/blog/shipping-gold-wash-plant-internationally/">duty</a> are worth planning before you order, not after.</p>
      <p>Not sure this is the right size? Compare it against the <a href="/products/300-ton/">300 Ton plant</a>, or read our guide to <a href="/blog/choosing-right-size-gold-wash-plant/">choosing the right size wash plant</a> for your ground.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
